    "dc.legislation.history" : [ {
      "value" : "Legislative History:\n The Repealing and Amending Act, 2023 \n\nSource: Official Record of Parliament, India Code, and Ministry of Law and Justice \n\nAct Title - The Repealing and Amending Act, 2023 \nAct Number - Act No. 37 of 2023 \nAct ID (India Code) - 202337\n Presidential Assent date - December 17, 2023 \n Enforcement Date - December 17, 2023 \nNodal Ministry - Ministry of Law and Justice \n\nPrecedent & Historical Rationale\n\n●\tPurging Obsolete and Redundant Laws: Formally repeals 65 obsolete and redundant enactments—including legacy amending Acts and outdated principal statutes—to clean up the statute book and eliminate statutory congestion.\n●\tCorrection of Minor Drafting and Technical Errors: Introduces minor typographical, formal, and textual corrections in the Factoring Regulation Act, 2011, without altering the substantive legal provisions or intent of the underlying law.\n \nParliamentary Trajectory & Enactment\n●\tFormulation: Introduced by the Union Minister of Law and Justice as part of the government's ongoing initiative to review, streamline, and periodically repeal unnecessary laws to enhance ease of living and administrative clarity.\n●\tParliamentary Passage: Introduced in the Lok Sabha on December 19, 2022; passed by the Lok Sabha on July 27, 2023; and passed by the Rajya Sabha on December 4, 2023.\n●\tPresidential Assent: Received the assent of the President of India on December 17, 2023.\n●\tEnforcement: Enforced on December 17, 2023 .",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
